# The kissing numbers, the count of spheres that can touch one central sphere in the record lattices. In four dimensions
# the D4 lattice reaches twenty-four, the vertices of the twenty-four-cell; in eight dimensions the E8 lattice reaches two
# hundred forty; in twenty-four dimensions the Leech lattice reaches one hundred ninety-six thousand five hundred sixty,
# each the proven maximum in its dimension. The minimal vectors always come in antipodal pairs, a vector and its negative,
# because a lattice is closed under negation, so the roots are organized by a sign that negation flips. This file MODELS
# that sign and DEFINES negation, then PROVES it is an involution, pairing every minimal vector with its opposite. The
# three record kissing numbers, and the decomposition of the Leech count into its three vector shapes, are recorded as
# machine-integer facts. The sign involution is proved over the actual sign type by induction.

# The sign of a minimal vector, flipped by negation, which pairs each root with its antipode.
form sign
  case positive
  case negative

# Negation, flipping the sign, sending each minimal vector to its antipodal partner.
task negate
  take s, like sign
  like sign
  fork case, read s
    case positive
      send back
        make negative
    case negative
      send back
        make positive

# NEGATION IS AN INVOLUTION: negating twice returns the sign, negate (negate s) = s, for every sign, so the minimal
# vectors come in antipodal pairs, a root and its opposite, and the kissing number is even. Proved by induction over the
# two signs.
rule negation-is-an-involution
  seat s, like sign
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate
        call negate
          read s
      read s
  fold s

# THE E8 KISSING NUMBER is two hundred forty, splitting as the integer-root family and the half-integer-root family,
# 240 = 112 + 128, as a machine-integer fact.
hold e-eight-kissing-splits-as-the-two-families
  call is-equal
    code 240
    call add
      code 112
      code 128

# THE D4 KISSING NUMBER is twenty-four, the rank times the Coxeter number, 4 * 6 = 24, the vertices of the twenty-four-
# cell.
hold d-four-kissing-is-twenty-four
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 4
      code 6

# THE LEECH KISSING NUMBER is one hundred ninety-six thousand five hundred sixty, the sum of its three vector shapes: the
# two-fours shape 1104, the octad shape 97152, and the one-three shape 98304, 1104 + 97152 + 98304 = 196560.
hold leech-kissing-splits-into-three-shapes
  call is-equal
    code 196560
    call add
      code 1104
      call add
        code 97152
        code 98304
